<title>FRANCE: Block of 1.33 percent in Canal Plus traded.</title>
<headline>Block of 1.33 percent in Canal Plus traded.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>A block of 328,000 shares in Canal Plus traded at 0803 GMT, which represents 1.33 percent of the share capital, at a price of 1,190 francs per share.</p>
<p>Market specialists said they believed the buyer was Cie Generale des Eaux and the seller either Caisse des Depots or Pathe. &quot;It's an operation by Generale des Eaux to counter the dilution that takes place with the merger of Canal Plus and Nethold,&quot; a trader said.</p>
<p>The Wall Street Journal said this morning that analysts were speculating Groupe Bruxelles Lambert might want to buy a stake and forge an alliance between Canal and CLT.</p>
</text>
